{"content":"🚨 **BLOCKING: `kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout` / `kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout` are never declared — the tree does not compile**

Commit a166c9f46 added the *doc comment* for the new network bounds but not the constants themselves. They are referenced at 9 sites across `bin/self_manage.dart`:

```dart
$ grep -n "kFaUpdate" bin/self_manage.dart
24:/// tag, manifest, signature) within [kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout]; the
25:/// archive body gets [kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout] (tens of MB on slow
290:        .timeout(kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout);
293:        .timeout(kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout);
432:    streamed = await client.send(request).timeout(kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout);
440:      bytes = await streamed.stream.toBytes().timeout(kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout);
668:    streamed = await client.send(request).timeout(kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout);
680:      .timeout(kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout);
803:  Duration networkTimeout = kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout,
894:        .timeout(kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout);
```

`Duration networkTimeout = kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout` (line 803) needs a compile-time constant; an undefined identifier there is a hard compile error. `bin/self_manage.dart` is `part of 'fah.dart'`, so the **whole `fa` CLI stops building**, and `test/cli/self_manage_test.dart` (which drives `applyUpdate`) fails to compile too. The generic language-analyze gates on this head are green only because the dart validation lane is parked for this guest PR — nothing on CI catches it; this must be fixed before merge.

Fix — declare what the doc comment promises (2 min per your own round-4 reply):

```dart
/// Metadata answers (latest tag, manifest, signature) must land within
/// this bound; slower means the update aborts, fail-closed.
const Duration kFaUpdateNetworkTimeout = Duration(seconds: 15);

/// The archive body bound (tens of MB on slow links).
const Duration kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout = Duration(minutes: 2);
```

A `dart analyze bin/self_manage.dart` (or letting the dart validation lane run) will confirm.
","path":"outputs/pr_review_comments/comment1.md"}

{"content":"⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the zip-fallback body timeout is uncaught — a slow archive still crashes `fa update` with a stack trace**

`fallbackZipUpdate` wraps its `send` in `try/on Exception` (line 668-674) but the very next leg is bare:

```dart
_say('extracting $zipAsset…');
final bytes = await streamed.stream
    .toBytes()
    .timeout(kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout); // ← no try/catch
```

Once the constants exist, an archive body that exceeds the bound throws `TimeoutException`, which propagates: `fallbackZipUpdate` → `_binaryUpdate` → `runSelfUpdate` (only a `finally`, no catch) → `exit(await runSelfUpdate(...))` in `fah_runapp.dart` — no catch → the zone handler prints `fa crashed: TimeoutException` and `exit(1)`. That is exactly the "a hung network there is a one-line failure, **never a stack trace**" behavior this commit claims for the manual legs; the macOS zip-fallback leg is the one path where it still isn't true. (Before this commit the leg simply waited — the new bound introduced the crash path.)

Mirror the `_binaryUpdate` pattern:

```dart
final List<int> bytes;
try {
  bytes = await streamed.stream.toBytes().timeout(kFaUpdateArchiveTimeout);
} on Exception catch (error) {
  _warn('download failed (network): $error');
  return 1;
}
```
