      a fast-failing or hostile network is INVISIBLE (no banner), never a
      crash; the banner also stands down once the TUI owns the terminal, so
      a 2-3 s answer cannot garble a live frame
    - the applyUpdate boot path is bounded end to end: the latest-tag fetch
      aborts through an injectable networkTimeout (default 15 s, null =>
      downloadFailed), the archive send/bytes get the network/archive bounds
      (TimeoutException lands in the existing catch-all => downloadFailed)
    - the same bounds cover the manual fa update download legs (binary +
      macOS zip fallback) — caught, warned, exit 1, never a stack trace
    - verifyReleaseProvenance's manifest+signature fetches are bounded too
      (fail-closed => provenanceFailed, nothing installed)
    - pub-global honesty: _pubGlobalUpdate returns the ACTIVATED version —
      'fa update applied' is only logged when pub actually advanced; a
      lagging pub.dev logs the real resolution and the same-binary respawn
      is skipped (convergenceGuard), not faked
    - tests: blackholed-network abort via an injectable 120 ms timeout;
      pub-global fake now differentiates list/activate so the activated-
      version parse is exercised

