{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: dead `await` on a `String` (`await_only_futures` analyzer info)**

```dart
final text = await (await env.readTextFile(_globalConfig)).getOrThrow();
```

`getOrThrow()` on the `Ok` case returns `String` synchronously — the outer `await` awaits a non-Future, which the analyzer flags (`await_only_futures`, test/config/auto_update_test.dart:213). It works today, but it misleads the reader into thinking `getOrThrow()` is async. Drop the outer `await`:

```dart
final text = (await env.readTextFile(_globalConfig)).getOrThrow();
```

Non-fatal for the CI gate (plain `dart analyze` — infos don't fail), just lint noise on a new line.
